s:bold>\n                    (2020), 44 pp., arXiv:1702.07957]) and show that the singularity category is the bounded derived category of the \u2010Tate spectrum (the \u2010nullification of the Koszul dual connective ring spectrum ). We establish a form of Gorenstein duality for , and show that the \u2010Tate spectrum enjoys a form of Tate duality. Under a complete intersection hypothesis we give a method for calculating the \u2010Tate homology.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1112\/blms.70405","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,1]],"date-time":"2026-06-01T14:38:35Z","timestamp":1780324715000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["The singularity category and duality for complete intersection groups"],"prefix":"10.1112","volume":"58","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-9855-3337","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"J. P. C.","family":"Greenlees","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Mathematics Institute Coventry UK"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,1]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_14_2_1","unstructured":"D. J.Benson Classifying spaces of finite groups of tame representation type Memoirs of the American Mathematical Society (to appear) arXiv:2208.07913."},{"key":"e_1_2_14_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1090\/S0002-9947-08-04728-4"},{"key":"e_1_2_14_4_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1112\/blms\/26.5.438"},{"key":"e_1_2_14_5_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.jpaa.2007.12.001"},{"key":"e_1_2_14_6_1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"D. J.BensonandJ. P. C.Greenlees The singularity and cosingularity categories for groups with cyclic Sylow subgroup Algebras and Representation Theory 26 1181\u20101216 arXiv:2107.09389 2021.","DOI":"10.1007\/s10468-022-10129-2"},{"key":"e_1_2_14_7_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher"